# Backend (Golang)

## Purpose

All server code is Go under `backend/`. Preserve Echo + PostgreSQL modular layout, thin handlers, service-layer domain logic, and ADR invariants.

## When it applies

Any change under `backend/**` (handlers, logic, dto, models, repositories, middlewares, routes, config, storage).

## Required practices

### Layout (do not invent parallel trees)

```
backend/api/handlers|middlewares
backend/internal/app/routes/v1/routes.go
backend/internal/dto
backend/internal/models
backend/internal/repositories
backend/internal/logic/{catalog,vehicle,media,aging}
backend/internal/services   # interfaces per domain + registry
backend/internal/common/{constant,errors}
backend/pkg/{config,database,storage,logger}
```

### Handlers

- Bind request DTOs, call `services.*()`, return `dto.Success` / `mapError`.
- Never embed inventory-age math, stock-out terminal rules, or VIN uniqueness in handlers.
- Separate routes for stock-out, proposed action, and primary image (ADR-0007).

### Services

- Put validation and domain rules in `internal/logic/**`.
- Aging and stock-state derivation belong in one place (e.g. `logic/aging` or `logic/vehicle` helpers) — frontend may display but must not redefine.
- Reuse typed app errors (`ErrValidation`, `ErrNotFound`, `ErrConflict`, …).

### Repositories

- All table access via `repositories.Store` / GORM.
- VIN uniqueness enforced at DB + service; stocked-out VIN never reused (ADR-0004, ADR-0006).

### Routes

Register in `internal/app/routes/v1/routes.go` only. Serve static UI + `/api` from one process in Compose (ADR-0009). Image GET streams bytes; never return MinIO URLs (ADR-0008).

### Responses

Always use the envelope:

```json
{ "code": 200, "message": "ok", "data": {}, "meta": null }
```

### Style

- Match neighboring files: early returns, calendar dates as `DATE` / `YYYY-MM-DD`, snake_case JSON tags.
- Module path: `inventory_dashboard/...` (or the module name in `go.mod`).

## Must never do

- Reopen a stocked-out vehicle to in stock, or allow a second vehicle with the same VIN.
- Accept free-text make/model; require catalog `model_id`.
- Put domain logic in `main.go`, middlewares, or DTOs.
- Publish MinIO or embed object URLs in vehicle JSON (report `has_primary_image` only).
- One PATCH that mixes stock-out, proposed action, and image (ADR-0007).

## Examples

```go
// ✅ Stock state from date
inStock := v.StockedOutOn == nil

// ❌ Persist StockState string alongside StockedOutOn
```

```go
// ✅ POST /vehicles/:id/stock-out → logic.Vehicle.StockOut
// ❌ PATCH /vehicles/:id { "stock_state": "stocked_out", "proposed_action": "hold", "image": ... }
```
